### Welcome to SEDS Mora

SEDS Mora is the student-led space exploration chapter based at the University of Moratuwa (UoM). Formed by passionate undergraduates across engineering, information technology, and related disciplines, our chapter provides a collaborative platform for students to explore space engineering, aerospace systems, robotics, and astronomy.

As a university chapter affiliated with SEDS Sri Lanka, SEDS Mora bridges classroom engineering theory with hands-on space exploration projects.

### What We Do

Members of SEDS Mora engage in team-based activities designed to build practical technical skills while having fun:

- **Space Robotics and Rover Prototypes**: Designing, 3D printing, and testing small ground rovers with rocker-bogie suspension systems, motor controllers, and sensor telemetry.
- **CanSat and Sensor Payloads**: Building micro-satellite models packed inside beverage cans to measure atmospheric pressure, altitude, and temperature during test drops and weather balloon flights.
- **Model Rocketry Study Circles**: Learning flight dynamics, aerodynamic stability simulations using OpenRocket, and electronic parachute ejection systems.
- **Workshops and Knowledge Sharing**: Conducting hands-on bootcamps for freshers on Arduino, Raspberry Pi, PCB design, CAD modeling, and orbital mechanics.
- **School Outreach and Mentorship**: Visiting schools across the Western Province to introduce young students to basic astronomy, water-bottle rocketry, and STEM careers.

### Community and Culture

At SEDS Mora, we believe space exploration is for everyone, whether you are in your first week of university or preparing your final-year research project. We foster a supportive team environment where senior students mentor newcomers and everyone learns by building together.

### How to Get Involved

Membership in SEDS Mora is completely free and open to all registered students of the University of Moratuwa.

- **Campus Recruitment**: Look out for our welcome sessions and recruitment calls at the beginning of the academic year.
- **Study Circles**: Join our weekly open discussion sessions on Discord and on-campus build nights.
- **Email**: [sedsmora@gmail.com](mailto:sedsmora@gmail.com)
